      "problem": "${g}^{″}(x)=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "Computing the first derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(8x-\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}) \\\\  & =8-\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot 3{x}^{2} \\\\  & =8-2{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, computing the second derivative, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{″}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(8-2{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =-4x.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
