    "q-166077": {
      "dom_id": "question-166077",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14199167/assets/5d2bfbefca5ce0a0b04accad183d0f43537d600c72000058b59f692398259a80.png)     \n                                \n                            \n\n   \n\n                            The graph of $y=g(x)$ for $x\\in [-3,3]$ is plotted above. In ascending order, what are the $x$-coordinates of the points on this interval where ${g}^{′}(x)=0?$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${g}^{′}(x)=0\\,$ when $\\,x\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,$ and $\\,x\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n.",
      "worked_solution": "A stationary point of $g(x)$ is a value of $x$ where ${g}^{′}(x)=0.$ Graphically, those are the values where the tangent to the graph is horizontal.  \n\nIn the given graph, we can see that at $x=-2$ and $x=2,$ the tangent to the graph is horizontal, so we have ${g}^{′}(x)=0$ at these points.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14199167/assets/36fd58470a5361250fa7852d92abe2b9c2dbf18ca97d00e51ea4013f8f3aa348.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, there are two stationary points, and their $x$-coordinates (in ascending order) are $x=-2$ and $x=2.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
